## THIS SECTION IS AN INTERACTIVE ACTIVITY
This section is an interactive adaptation of a printed activity: the learner answers digitally instead of writing on the paper page. Interactive elements (inputs, textareas, radio/checkbox options, buttons, feedback areas, `[[blank:...]]` markers) are REQUIRED and intentionally absent from the original page image.
- NEVER remove, hide, or disable an interactive element to better match the print layout.
- NEVER restyle an interactive element to imitate a static print affordance (a blank writing line, a hand-drawn checkbox, a dotted answer space). Controls must remain recognisably interactive.
- Keep every class and attribute the activity runtime depends on (for example `data-activity-item`, option and label classes, `aria-label`s) exactly as they appear in the current HTML. Restyle around them; never remove or rename them.
- Editable fields that replace printed blanks, auto-numbered items, and answer-checking chrome are correct and expected — do not flag them as extraneous or missing from the original.
- The fidelity target for an activity is the book's design language — palette, typography hierarchy, borders, badges, instruction layout, and imagery — applied to the interactive layout. Do NOT compare the controls element-for-element against the print page.
